  ('SynchronousMachine', 'ikk', true, 'CurrentFlow', NULL, 'Steady-state short-circuit current (in A for the profile) of generator with compound excitation during 3-phase short circuit. - Ikk=0: Generator with no compound excitation. - Ikk?0: Generator with compound excitation. Ikk is used to calculate the minimum steady-state short-circuit current for generators with compound excitation (Section 4.6.1.2 in the IEC 60909-0) Used only for single fed short circuit on a generator. (Section 4.3.4.2. in the IEC 60909-0)', 'schema/cim/IEC_CIM.ttl'),
